'''The Void''' is a [[chapter]] added in ''[[Afterbirth+]]''. It is unlocked by defeating {{e|Hush}}. '''The Void''' is one of five final levels in ''The Binding of Isaac'', alongside the {{s|Chest}}, the {{s|Dark Room}}, the {{s|Corpse}}, and {{s|Home}}.

Each room in this chapter takes the form of a different chapter, ranging from the {{s|Basement}} to the {{s|Chest}} and the {{s|Dark Room}}, including variant chapters like the {{s|Cellar}} and the {{s|Burning Basement}}. The Void is extremely large compared to other floors, and it is the only floor in the game (not counting XL floors) to contain multiple boss rooms. Most of them contain random bosses from other floors, including some of the final bosses, such as {{e|It Lives!}}, {{e|Satan}}, {{e|Isaac}}, etc. One of them, however, contains the main boss of the floor, which is always {{e|Delirium}}.

Monsters encountered in The Void have a much higher chance of appearing as Champions.

{{dlc|r}} The {{e|Portal}} monster is exclusive to this floor, and all rooms in which it would have been previously encountered on other chapters now only generate on this floor.

== Access ==
After defeating Hush at least once, a new exit will appear in the upper right-hand corner of the 2x2 boss room in which Hush was fought. The new room contains nothing except for a Portal. It does not spawn enemies and serves as the entrance to The Void.

After unlocking The Void, the portal can then appear after every major boss starting with {{e|Mom}}, even if Hush was not defeated in that run.

The deeper the boss, the higher the spawning chance:
* 5% after {{e|Mom}} (Only if Isaac has 10+ tear damage or 20+ items)
* 10% after {{e|Mom's Heart}} / {{e|It Lives!}}
* 15% after {{e|Isaac}} or {{e|Satan}}
* {{dlc|nr+}} 20% after {{e|???}} or {{e|The Lamb}}
* {{dlc|nr+}} 50% after {{e|Mega Satan}} (If the portal appears, the run will not end instantly like it normally does)
* Defeating {{e|Hush}} will guarantee entrance to The Void.
** {{dlc|r+}} Defeating {{e|???}}, {{e|The Lamb}}, {{e|Mega Satan}}, or {{e|Mother|n}} will also guarantee a portal.

=== Notes ===
* The portal can appear multiple times during a single run.
** {{dlc|nr+}} The chance for at least one portal to open after fighting It Lives!, Isaac/Satan, and {{e|???}}/{{e|The Lamb}} is 38.8%.<ref>Chance = 1 - (1-0.10)(1-0.15)(1-0.20) = 1 - 0.9*0.85*0.80 = 0.388</ref>
** {{dlc|nr+}} If {{e|Mega Satan}} is defeated, the chance for at least one portal increases to 69.4%.
* If a portal appears after Mega Satan, a big chest will appear alongside it. Jumping into the chest will end the run normally.
* {{Dlc|nr}} If the portal spawns below Isaac's position after defeating a boss, he will immediately enter The Void.
* {{dlc|nr}} Jumping into a trapdoor will reset The Void, an effect identical to {{i|Forget Me Now}}. This is useful if it has already been explored, but the player wants to clear more rooms to acquire health items before the final fight. The trapdoor must be found via a black market under rocks, as {{i|We Need To Go Deeper!}} and {{p|Ehwaz}} won't work.
* {{dlc|nr}} Similarly, going to an {{r|I AM ERROR}} Room in The Void allows Isaac to reset the floor, so teleport items like {{i|Undefined}} can let Isaac repeat The Void multiple times.
* {{dlc|r}} The {{r|I AM ERROR}} room can be reached by leaving a {{r|Crawl Space}} through an unintended direction in the {{s|Chest}} and the {{s|Dark Room}}. The room will always contain a portal leading to The Void. However, any other method of getting to the {{r|I AM ERROR}} room will fail and generate an I am Error shopkeeper instead. Thus, the likelihood of this ever happening is practically zero without using items that can force the generation of the Crawl Space trapdoor, such as {{i|We Need To Go Deeper!}}
* {{Dlc|r}} If the portal appears after Mom and the player chooses the [[Ascent]] path, the portal will still visually spawn on the way up. However, it is closed and can not be interacted with.
* Once the Portal Entrance to the Void is spawned in a Boss Room, it will stay open even after leaving the room.

