This floor contains multiple boss rooms, only one of which will contain Delirium. The other boss rooms contain a random boss from any floor including final bosses, except {{e|Mom}}, {{e|Mega Satan}}, {{e|Hush}}, {{e|Ultra Greed}}, {{e|Mother}}, {{e|Dogma}}, the [[Harbingers (Bosses)|Ultra Harbingers]], {{e|The Beast}}, and all ''[[Repentance]]'' bosses that only appear on the alternate path.

=== Notes ===
* Delirium's boss room is a 2x2 room, but appears as a 1x1 room on the minimap.
** Similarly, {{e|Mr. Fred}}'s 1x2 room will appear as a 1x1 room if he spawns.
** {{dlc+|r}} Unlike normal boss rooms, {{r|Red Room}}s can be created adjacent to these non-appearing rooms.{{dlc-}}
* Items awarded from defeating bosses in The Void are generated as if {{i|Chaos|n}} was active, drawing from any [[item pool]].
** If rerolled, the new items use the [[Boss (Item Pool)|Boss item pool]].
* Since the Void has multiple boss rooms, using {{p|IV - The Emperor}} will teleport Isaac to one of them randomly.
* Defeating a final boss in The Void that is not Delirium will not give a [[Completion Mark]] of that boss and will not unlock the respective item. It will however count towards other unlocks, like {{e|Triachnid}} for killing {{e|Isaac}}.

=== Locating Delirium ===
{{Main|The Void/Locating Delirium}}
* To locate boss rooms which will most likely contain Delirium, Isaac must look at the boss rooms on the map:
** Try to find a boss room that would not be connected to other rooms if it was a 2x2 room. If it would connect, the room won't contain Delirium.
** Remember that the boundaries of the map are at a maximum of 13x13 squares. If a 2x2 boss room would extend past those boundaries, that room cannot contain Delirium.
* By knowing which boss rooms cannot contain Delirium, Isaac can safely enter certain boss rooms to gather items before fighting Delirium, or not enter these boss rooms knowing that Delirium is not there.
* Entering boss rooms with a teleport card is also smart in case you encounter Delirium.

