== Trivia ==
* It is implied that the different forms (floors from chapters 1 to 6) of this floor are just Isaac's hallucinations, as the Void's icon on the progress bar (after advancing to the next floor) is a red vortex, and the "floor" graphic (below the player character and bosses in "VS" screens) is a red vortex as well.
* On [[Isaac's last will]], The Void is referred to as "some dying memory".
* Occasionally, there will be a static distortion and the background and objects of the room may change to those of other chapters.
* {{e|Mom's Heart}} can still spawn as a boss, even after being replaced by It Lives! in [[Chapter 4]].
* {{dlc|nr}} The Void is the only floor that can be cleared indefinitely with {{i|Undefined}} (or {{i|Teleport 2.0}} plus {{i|The Battery}} or a guaranteed {{e|Lil' Battery}} drop).
* The champion enemies spawned in The Void will never drop any of their assigned drops.
* {{dlc|nr}} The Void can be entered in [[Greed Mode]] by entering "stage 8" in the [[Debug Console]]. The rooms have random backdrops and the music is the same as The Void in regular mode, but the boss is {{e|Ultra Greed}} and will drop the Final Boss Chest. Entering the chest will play Ending 20 instead of Ending 18 or 19.
** {{dlc|r}} The "stage 8" floor has no name, no music and plays no ending when entering the Chest.
* The starting room and the boss rooms of The Void do not have the visual effects of the environment they're based on (i.e. a boss room with a Womb backdrop will not have the red static of the {{s|Womb}}).
** {{dlc|nr}} Also, Caves-based rooms do not have the visual effects of {{s|Caves}}.
* Even if a boss isn't unlocked (i.e. {{e|Sisters Vis}} before beating {{e|???}} 6 times), it can still appear in one of the boss rooms.
* {{dlc|r}} An unused floor found in ''Repentance'' sharing the name "The Void" can be found in the game's files and contains a variety of unique unimplemented rooms, some of which feature ''Repentance'' bosses.
** This may have been related to the Delirium revamp which Kilburn noted in a tweet.<ref>https://twitter.com/fixitvinh/status/1251434846011998208</ref>
* {{dlc|r}} As of [[Repentance]], The Void is the only chapter in which the boss VS screen is completely black, as opposed to having a slightly coloured shade to represent the current chapter/environment Isaac is in.

== Music ==
* The [[music]] that plays in The Void is titled ''Terminus''.<ref>[https://ridiculon.bandcamp.com/album/the-binding-of-isaac-afterbirth-ost-2 Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth+ OST]</ref>
** The track appears to be a remix of Crusade, Genesis 22:10 (title screen), and the {{s|Basement}} and the {{s|Burning Basement}} themes.
*** This may be inspired by the Void's theme in Antibirth, which was a mashup of several floor tracks in the game.

